@startuml dict-pipeline
' The two ways to obtain a dictionary in libgrammstein:
' (a) the standalone path — WordExtractor ⇒ DictionaryBuilder ⇒ SpellingDictionary;
' (b) the zero-copy path — VocabularyDictionary over an existing n-gram model.
' Render: plantuml -tsvg docs/diagrams/dict-pipeline.puml
' Source of truth for Figure 1 in docs/components/dictionary/overview.md, section "Two dictionaries, one interface".
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam rectangle {
  FontColor white
  FontStyle bold
  BorderColor #263238
  roundCorner 12
}
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowFontColor #37474F
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #E3F2FD
  BorderColor #1565C0
}
title The two dictionary paths — standalone extraction vs. the vocabulary already in the model

rectangle "**CorpusReader::sentences()**" as corpus #546E7A

rectangle "**(a) WordExtractor**\nDashMap<String, u64, SafeGxBuildHasher>\nAtomicU64 total_tokens · AtomicUsize sentences\nadd_sentence(&self) — shared-reference writes" as wx #00838F
rectangle "**ExtractionConfig**\nmin/max_word_length · lowercase\nfilter_digits · filter_special" as cfg #1565C0
rectangle "**entries_filtered(min_frequency)**\nVec<WordEntry> with log_prob = ln(f / N)" as filt #1565C0
rectangle "**DictionaryBuilder**\nmin_frequency · language · source\ncompute_log_probs" as db #1565C0
rectangle "**SpellingDictionary**\nentries : Vec<WordEntry> (sorted by f, descending)\nword_index : HashMap<String, usize> (rebuilt on load)\nmetadata : DictionaryMetadata" as sd #00838F

rectangle "**words.dict**\nb“DICT” + version + bincode\n(feature: serde-extras)" as bin #00838F
rectangle "**words.txt**\nword \\t frequency — always available" as txt #00838F

rectangle "**(b) n-gram training**\nSharedConcurrentVocab + NgramStorage" as ng #1565C0
rectangle "**VocabularyDictionary**\nborrows the vocabulary and the unigram counts\n(feature: google-books)" as vd #00838F

rectangle "**Consumers** — spell check · candidate ranking · Levenshtein automata" as cons #455A64

corpus --> wx : add_sentence(s)
cfg --> wx : normalize_word
wx --> filt : f(w) ≥ min_frequency
filt --> db
db --> sd : build_from_extractor\n· build_from_counts
sd --> bin : save()
sd --> txt : export_text()
bin --> sd : load()
txt --> sd : import_text()
sd --> cons : contains · frequency · log_prob · rank · top_n

corpus --> ng
ng --> vd : new(vocab, &storage)
vd --> cons : contains · frequency

note right of wx
  **Not a trie.** The extractor is a sharded concurrent hash
  map and the finished dictionary is a Vec plus a HashMap.
  No DoubleArrayTrie, no PathMap, no PersistentARTrie is
  constructed anywhere in src/dictionary.
end note

note bottom of vd
  **Prefer (b) when an n-gram model already exists**: the vocabulary
  holds every word and storage holds the unigram counts, so a second
  copy buys nothing. frequency(w) is Some only when w is in the
  vocabulary **and** carries a stored unigram count; call
  storage.sync_vocabulary() first, or lock-free inserts stay invisible.
end note

legend right
  |= Colour |= Role |
  |<#546E7A> | corpus I-O |
  |<#1565C0> | statistical core / configuration |
  |<#00838F> | storage & persistence |
  |<#455A64> | consumers |
endlegend
@enduml
